     There's more code below the excerpt you quoted, and it applies
to the case where Stormbringer is already in hard.  The enchantment
gets set to +1 if it was lower, left as is if already +1 or better.
The weapon is blessed; any rust/corrosion/&c is repaired; it becomes
rustproof/corrodeproof/&c; the blessed/cursed status and rustproofing
status are marked as known so get shown in inventory display.  And if
the weapon skill is currently restricted (locked at unskilled, that
is), the restriction is removed making it eligible to be trained up
to basic.  (The last bit is relevant to the "already wielding" case
mentioned next; for Excalibur/Vorpal Blade/Stormbringer, their
corresponding skill gets unlocked in the section of code you showed
and the subsequent unlocking becomes redundant.)

     Not a general +1 but certainly more than nothing.  It applies to
any weapon you get from the crowning, or to whatever weapon you're
already wielding if you don't get one (unless you're a wizard or a
monk who gets the spellbook for a spell you don't already know, in
which case your weapon is ignored).  If you don't receive a weapon
(or a book for not yet known spell) and aren't wielding a weapon:
"you feel unworthy".


